{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nIndependent review of ticket 5f4d found two non-blocking hardening gaps in\nscripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py. A file containing invalid UTF-8 is skipped wholesale\n(`except UnicodeDecodeError: continue`), so a source file can evade the guard by carrying one\nbad byte. Separately, an unallowlisted match prints the complete raw source line, so a very\nlong line or embedded control characters land unescaped in CI logs.\n\n## Plan\n- Define a source-ish text extension set (`.py`, `.md`, `.json`, `.yaml`/`.yml`, `.toml`) that\n  must FAIL CLOSED on a decode error, while every other extension stays tolerated so genuine\n  binaries do not produce false positives.\n- Bound and escape diagnostic excerpts: escape non-printable characters and cap the excerpt at\n  a documented maximum length, with an explicit truncation marker.\n- Add behavioral tests for invalid-byte source input, invalid-byte binary input, and\n  hostile (long / control-character) matching lines.\n\n## Testing\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_check_criteria_vocabulary.py -q` — new cases: an\n  undecodable `.py` exits 1 naming the file, an undecodable `.bin` exits 0, and a long\n  control-character line is emitted escaped and truncated.\n- `make lint` and `make typecheck` — the guard is itself part of the `make lint` gate, so a\n  clean run proves the real repository still scans clean.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Known text files cannot evade the vocabulary guard by containing an invalid UTF-8 byte:\n      verified by a test asserting exit 1 and the offending path in stderr.\n- [ ] Binary files remain safely ignored without false positives: verified by a test asserting\n      exit 0 for an undecodable non-source extension.\n- [ ] Diagnostics escape control characters and cap source excerpts at a documented maximum\n      length: verified by a test asserting no raw control byte and a truncation marker in stderr.\n- [ ] `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_check_criteria_vocabulary.py -q` and `make lint` pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786500281472538001,"uuid":"deaa9db7-40b4-4ead-b3d5-45944ffdb1d7"}